NUM-17: count every barrel in the outflow from a storage unit (KW, SF)

Under KINWAVE and STEADY routing, storage_getOutflow() gives the flow from
a storage unit into a conduit as the conduit's normal flow at the storage
depth, or its full flow once the storage is deeper than the conduit. Both
Link.qFull and Conduit.beta are per barrel, but the caller treats the
result as the conduit's total inflow (kinwave_execute() and
steadyflow_execute() divide it by the barrel count), so a multi-barrel
outlet passed the flow of one barrel. Multiply both results by the number
of barrels. Single-barrel conduits are unchanged.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply NUM-17_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/node.c b/src/legacy/engine/node.c
index 070db5a..12c41f9 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/node.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/node.c
@@ -1024,13 +1024,14 @@ double storage_getOutflow(int j, int i)
     y = Node[j].newDepth - Link[i].offset1;
 
     // --- return 0 if conduit empty or full flow if full
+    //     (qFull and beta are per barrel)
+    k = Link[i].subIndex;
     if ( y <= 0.0 ) return 0.0;
-    if ( y >= Link[i].xsect.yFull ) return Link[i].qFull;
+    if ( y >= Link[i].xsect.yFull ) return Link[i].qFull * Conduit[k].barrels;
 
     // --- if partially full, return normal flow
-    k = Link[i].subIndex;
     a = xsect_getAofY(&Link[i].xsect, y);
-    return Conduit[k].beta * xsect_getSofA(&Link[i].xsect, a);
+    return Conduit[k].beta * xsect_getSofA(&Link[i].xsect, a) * Conduit[k].barrels;
 }
 
 //=============================================================================
